SUMMARY:"Persuasion" - A One Act Play Inspired by Jane Austen
DESCRIPTION:“Persuasion” relates the story of Anne Elliot\, an aristocratic young lady who declines marrying Captain Frederick Wentworth at a youthful age even though she deeply loves him.  After a period of seven years\, Anne and Wentworth meet again and must resolve their feelings through a series of encounters that are highlighted in the play.  This one-act play\, inspired by scenes from Jane Austen’s novel\, was adapted for Historic Rock Ford by Samuel Slaymaker. . \n\n\n\nPerformance Dates: November 6\, 7 \, 13\,14\, 21 from 7-8:30 PM ; November 22 from 2-3:30 PM Where: First floor of the Circa 1794 General Hand Mansion. \n\n\n\nDue to space constraints within the rooms of the Hand Mansion\, audiences are limited to 15 guests per performance.  Guests are standing for the entire performance and will be moving from room to room following the action of the play. Tickets must be purchased in advance through ticketing link. Due to limited space for each performance\, tickets will not be available at the door \n\n\n\n\n\n\n    Buy Tickets
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/persuasion-a-one-act-play-inspired-by-jane-austen/
LOCATION:Historic Rock Ford\, 881 ROCKFORD RD\, Lancaster\, 17602
CATEGORIES:Arts & Entertainment
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://fig.guide/content/uploads/sites/3/2026/08/Persuasion-at-Historic-Rock-Ford-scaled.avif
ORGANIZER;CN="Historic Rock Ford":MAILTO:office@historicrockford.org
END:VEVENT
